  id: the_lodger
  title: The Lodger
  sceneName: Case_Lodger
  entity: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7158d2ec6b38cb14e83c4a15df35c67d, type: 2}
  clues:
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: e16a08d801437dc40a61578abad86c74, type: 2}
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8b05b7f413d2b544f9d59bf662c68bcc, type: 2}
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 40545d1ec1090d744948e2df590ac92a, type: 2}
  isFinal: 0
  edition: "Baku  \xB7  Sunday edition  \xB7  Vol. XII, No. 206"
  flavorHeadlines:
  - Hotel Occupancy Hits Record High
  - Airport Delays Continue Into Second Week
  - Lost Luggage Auction Draws Crowds
  leadHeadline: 'Caravanserai Inn: Room 9 Guest "Never Checked Out". Staff Report
    Warm Room, Untouched Bed'
  leadDetail: Light under the door reported at 3 AM, Old City.
  leadReaction:
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: A guest who never checks out. Funny thing to read in a hotel room.
  arrivalLines:
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: Caravanserai Inn, room nine. Warm in here. Lived-in, without the living.
  bookRevealLines: []
  identifyLines:
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: The Lodger. Takes a room, keeps it, forgets it was ever going anywhere.
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: ...The fix isn't written. The ink just stops.
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: Fine. It signs the register under a name that isn't its own. Strike the
      name, with the pen it signed with.
  wrongToolLine: I try the {0}. Down the hall a key turns in a lock. It's not going
    anywhere.
  resolveLines:
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: One line through the name, in its own ink.
  - speaker: 
    text: The ink runs. The room cools. Somewhere a clock starts ticking again.
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: Checkout's at noon, friend.
